{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.QSerreCriticalPairs","@type":"LeanModule","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.QSerreCriticalPairs","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.NormalForms"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.contextMul_four_coeffEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.contextMul_four_coeffEq","kind":"theorem","line":299,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/QSerreCriticalPairs.lean#L299-L326","doc":"The four-term counterpart. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.contextMul_two_coeffEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.contextMul_two_coeffEq","kind":"theorem","line":277,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/QSerreCriticalPairs.lean#L277-L297","doc":"`a · (c₁·m₁ + c₂·m₂) · b = c₁·(a m₁ b) + c₂·(a m₂ b)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.context_cancel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.context_cancel","kind":"theorem","line":270,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/QSerreCriticalPairs.lean#L270-L275","doc":"Cancelling a common context on both sides. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerre_overlap_enumeration","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerre_overlap_enumeration","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/QSerreCriticalPairs.lean#L189-L238","doc":"**Exactly eight ordered rule pairs admit a length-1 overlap, and here they\nare.**\n\nOf the 49 ordered pairs, 41 admit none: a length-1 overlap forces\n`lm₁ = [a,b]` and `lm₂ = [b,c]` sharing the letter `b`, and for those 41 the\nsecond letter of `lm₁` differs from the first of `lm₂`, so the decomposition\nequations are contradictory.\n\nThis reproduces, inside Lean, the enumeration\n`computations/qserre_gs_basis_check.py` arrived at symbolically — the two agree\nthat there are 8, and on which 8. Bean qou-18s7 verified that all 8 resolve;\nthe reduction chains witnessing that are what remains (§6). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerre_is_gs_basis_of_critical_pairs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerre_is_gs_basis_of_critical_pairs","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/QSerreCriticalPairs.lean#L158-L184","doc":"**`qSerre_is_gs_basis` follows from the length-1 critical pairs alone.**\n\nThis is the point of the file. `IsGrobnerShirshovBasis` quantifies over\n*every* overlap and inclusion composition, which is an unbounded-looking\nobligation; §§2–3 show that all of it is degenerate except the overlaps whose\noverlap is a single letter. So the axiom's entire content is the hypothesis\n`hcp` below — and bean qou-18s7's computation says there are exactly **8**\nsuch ambiguities and all 8 resolve.\n\nDischarging `hcp` therefore discharges `qSerre_is_gs_basis` outright, and\n`hcp` is 8 explicit two-step reduction chains rather than an open question\nabout the algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerre_overlap_resolves_of_length_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerre_overlap_resolves_of_length_two","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/QSerreCriticalPairs.lean#L139-L154","doc":"**The degenerate overlap case resolves.** When the overlap is the whole of\nboth leading monomials the two rules coincide, and the S-polynomial is a\ndifference of an element with itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerre_overlap_shape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerre_overlap_shape","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/QSerreCriticalPairs.lean#L113-L137","doc":"**Only two shapes are possible.** `overlap ≠ []` plus length-2 leading\nmonomials leaves `|overlap| = 1` (the genuine critical pairs, with `left` and\n`right` single letters) or `|overlap| = 2` (degenerate: the two rules lead on\nthe same word). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerre_inclusion_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerre_inclusion_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/QSerreCriticalPairs.lean#L80-L109","doc":"**`inclusion_resolves`, discharged.**\n\nBoth leading monomials have length 2, and `outer.lm = left ++ inner.lm ++\nright`, so `left` and `right` are empty on length grounds alone. Then\n`outer.lm = inner.lm`, so `outer = inner` by §1, and the S-polynomial is a\ndifference of an element with itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerre_rule_eq_of_lm_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerre_rule_eq_of_lm_eq","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/QSerreCriticalPairs.lean#L63-L76","doc":"**A rule of the system is determined by its leading monomial** — the seven\nare pairwise distinct. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerre_lm_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerre_lm_length","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/QSerreCriticalPairs.lean#L55-L61","doc":"**Every q-Serre leading monomial is a two-letter word.** ","signatureChunk":0}]}